ader changed to 'Showing results for \\\"keyboard\\\"' and displayed only the single matching thread \\\"Building a mechanical keyboard from scratch\\\" whose title and body contain the keyword, correctly filtering out all other unrelated threads.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked \\\"Technology\\\" category link; navigated to /category/tech which displays only 2 threads both tagged \\\"Technology\\\" (\\\"Building a mechanical keyboard from scratch\\\" and \\\"What programming language should I learn in 2024?\\\"), correctly excluding threads from other categories.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Homepage has Trending/Recent/Most Active tabs. \\\"Trending\\\" sorts by upvotes descending (156,124,92,89...). Clicking \\\"Most Active\\\" changed heading to \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\" and reordered list by reply count descending (89,67,45,41,38,34,31,23,2 replies), correctly reflecting recent activity/interaction frequency.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Reply history not shown\", \"actual\": \"Profile page only displays a \\\"Threads by qatester2026 (1)\\\" section listing threads the user started. Despite the user having posted 3 replies (verified in earlier steps), there is no \\\"Replies by\\\" section, tab, or any other UI element showing the user's reply history. Only thread-starting history is viewable, not the full posting and reply history.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked on \\\"TechExplorer\\\" author link from a thread; navigated to /profile/user-1 showing their public profile: bio (\\\"Full-stack developer passionate about open source...\\\"), interest tags (Programming, Open Source, AI/ML, DevOps), join date, reputation, and their thread history.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No edit feature for posts/replies\", \"actual\": \"Inspected the thread and reply DOM for edit/delete controls (buttons, icons, menus) on content authored by the logged-in user; none exist. Only an upvote button, reply-count icon, and view-count icon are present per post. Since there is no way to edit a published thread or reply, there is no \\\"Edited\\\" mark or last-edit-time feature to verify.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No rich text editing support\", \"actual\": \"The thread composer is a plain textarea with no formatting toolbar (no bold/link/list buttons). Entered markdown-style content \\\"**bold**\\\", \\\"[link](https://example.com)\\\", and a \\\"- item\\\" list rendered as literal raw text on the published thread page (e.g. \\\"This is a **bold** statement with a [link](https://example.com) and a list: - item one - item two - item three\\\") instead of being rendered as bold text, a clickable hyperlink, or a bulleted list.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Logged out (nav switched to Login/Register) and logged back in with qatester2026@example.com; toast \\\"Welcome back!\\\" shown. Verified profile page still showed bio \\\"QA engineer who loves testing forums...\\\" and interest tags (Testing, Gaming, Hiking), thread history \\\"Threads by qatester2026 (1)\\\" still listed, and the thread/reply page showed unchanged vote counts (thread upvote=1, first reply upvote=1) matching the pre-logout state, confirming state was correctly restored.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"Create Thread\\\" with empty category/title/content triggered toast warning \\\"Please fill in all fields\\\" and submission was blocked (stayed on /new-thread).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No